From: Nick Atkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 9 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mdrv2: don't report the inventory startup race as an error

systemInfoUpdate() looks up the Inventory anchor object that SMBIOS
content hangs off. At BMC startup that object does not exist yet -- the
configuration provider (entity-manager) publishes it only after it has
probed FRUs, which on this board takes ~25 seconds after smbios-mdr
starts. The lookup therefore throws ResourceNotFound and motherboardPath
comes back empty, producing three error lines per boot:

    Exception while trying to find Inventory anchor object for SMBIOS content ...
    Failed to query system motherboard: ...
    Failed to get system motherboard dbus path. Setting up a match rule

None of them indicates a fault. The code immediately installs an
interfacesAdded match rule for exactly this case and recovers on its own:

    Successful match on system interface
    Found Inventory anchor object for SMBIOS content ...: /xyz/.../board/...

So the normal path emits three errors and then quietly succeeds, which
trains you to ignore smbios-mdr's error output.

Report the absent anchor at debug (the two catch-block lines said the
same thing twice, so fold them into one), and keep the fallback itself at
info rather than dropping it entirely -- on a board where the anchor never
appears, that line is the only breadcrumb explaining why SMBIOS inventory
stayed empty.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Nick Atkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/src/mdrv2.cpp b/src/mdrv2.cpp
index a6cd342..59e4b95 100644
--- a/src/mdrv2.cpp
+++ b/src/mdrv2.cpp
@@ -435,17 +435,23 @@ void MDRV2::systemInfoUpdate()
     }
     catch (const sdbusplus::exception_t& e)
     {
-        lg2::error(
-            "Exception while trying to find Inventory anchor object for SMBIOS content {I}: {E}",
+        // Not an error: this runs at startup, and the inventory subtree does
+        // not exist until the configuration provider (entity-manager) has
+        // published it, which can be tens of seconds later. The match rule
+        // installed below is what handles that, so report at debug and let the
+        // fallback do its job.
+        lg2::debug(
+            "Inventory anchor object for SMBIOS content {I} not present yet: {E}",
             "I", smbiosInventoryPath, "E", e.what());
-        lg2::error("Failed to query system motherboard: {ERROR}", "ERROR",
-                   e.what());
     }
 
     if (motherboardPath.empty())
     {
-        lg2::error(
-            "Failed to get system motherboard dbus path. Setting up a match rule");
+        // Deliberate fallback, not a failure -- kept at info so that a board
+        // where the anchor never appears still leaves a breadcrumb explaining
+        // why SMBIOS inventory is empty.
+        lg2::info(
+            "System motherboard dbus path not available yet. Setting up a match rule");
 
         if (motherboardConfigMatch)
         {
